Package: smartune
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Intel Corporation <smartune@intel.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-bpfcc, openssl, xdg-utils, policykit-1|polkitd, curl, git, iproute2, iptables, iotop, kmod
Recommends: cpuid, msr-tools, linux-headers-generic, cpupower
Conflicts: smartune-monitor
Replaces: smartune-monitor
Provides: smartune-monitor
Description: Intel XPU SmarTune (Balancer + Monitor)
 Full Intel XPU SmarTune product: the system-pressure/telemetry monitoring
 dashboard together with the balancer (eBPF app interception, cgroup/CPU/memory/
 IO/network governance) running as one service.
 .
 Also includes the model-benchmark toolchain behind the dashboard's Benchmark
 tab. Only its scripts are packaged; the Python environment, model downloads and
 conversion outputs are built on first use under
 /opt/intel/smartune/benchmark/runtime and need internet access and tens of GB of
 disk (git and curl are pulled in for that). Set benchmark.env_root in
 config.yaml to place them on another volume, or benchmark.enabled to false to
 hide the tab entirely.
 .
 Installs a desktop launcher (application menu + desktop icon) that starts the
 combined service on demand and opens the dashboard in the default browser at
 https://localhost:9001. Not started at boot; runs only while in use.
 .
 The balancer needs the BCC/eBPF Python bindings (python3-bpfcc) and matching
 kernel headers (linux-headers-*) so its eBPF programs compile at runtime, plus
 iproute2, iptables, iotop and kmod for network/IO control. cpupower is
 recommended for CPU frequency and governor control but is not required. This
 package supersedes and conflicts with smartune-monitor.
